      "schema_version": "aspr_gear",
      "text": "This study tests whether Syngap1 loss alters murine neocortical progenitor behavior and cellular output. Across embryonic progenitor, division, proliferation, neuronal, and glial readouts, it reports no major genotype-associated differences, thereby providing a direct mouse counterpoint to earlier human-organoid and Xenopus findings. The final-state record preserves a residual scope limitation: the data do not resolve why models differ or exclude effects in less-represented progenitor populations and developmental contexts."
    },
